		"notes": {
			"techniques": "The eggs poach in the reduced sauce under a lid, so steam sets the tops of the whites.",
			"chemistry": "Egg white sets around 62–65 °C and yolk thickens around 65–70 °C, which is why a short, gentle cook leaves the yolk runny. Reducing the sauce concentrates its sugars and acids.",
